  "message": "Sure thing. The browser‑opener tool is just a tiny piece of code that tells the computer to launch whatever web browser you have installed, with a web address or a search term you give it. Think of it like pressing a “open webpage” button – the tool hands the address to the operating system, and the OS starts the browser for you. Right now the mechanic found that part of the code can’t even be loaded because a small support file is missing, so the whole thing is broken. Fixing it just means copying that missing file into the right place so the tool can be imported and work again.",
